{
  "sheet": "power-usb",
  "title": "Aius carrier - power-usb sheet",
  "paper": "A3",
  "global_nets": ["GND", "VBUS_5V"],
  "description": [
    "Sole power entry for the Aius carrier: rear USB-C VBUS -> TPS2553",
    "current-limited / reverse-blocking load switch -> protected 5V rail ->",
    "internal USB-A receptacle (and downstream Teensy via the internal cable).",
    "Sink-only USB 2.0: CC1/CC2 have independent 5.1k Rd pulldowns; D+/D- are a",
    "single 90-ohm differential pair from USB-C through the TPD2EUSB30A shunt ESD",
    "to the USB-A receptacle. No path sources USB VBUS; no second 5V feed."
  ],
  "design_notes": {
    "en_default": "TPS2553 EN is active-high. R3 (10k) pulls EN up to VBUS_RAW so the load switch is ENABLED by default at plug-in, with no controller on this domain - the protected rail comes up from hardware alone.",
    "ilim": "R4 (24.9k, 1%) sets the current-limit threshold. Per the TPS2553 datasheet range (15k..232k over 1.7A..75mA), ~24.9k yields a ~1.0A limit: comfortably above the Teensy plus a bus-powered internal USB device (<0.6A typical) while protecting the USB-C source.",
    "fault": "FAULT is active-low open-drain. R5 (100k) pulls it up to VBUS_RAW so it reads deasserted when healthy; it is a monitor-only output on this sheet (no consumer).",
    "decoupling": "C1 100nF + C2 10uF bulk on VBUS_RAW at the switch input; C3 100nF + C4 10uF on the protected VBUS_5V output feeding the USB-A port.",
    "shield": "USB-C and USB-A shells share the CHASSIS net (chassis-shield domain), kept separate from GND per the interfaces-and-states backfeed rule.",
    "usb_c_part": "USB-C receptacle candidate GCT USB4105-GF-A (16-pin USB2.0); D+/D- A- and B-side pins are tied for reversibility. SBU1/SBU2 unused (no-connect)."
  },
